Critic review saved to `docs/content-analysis/perspective-reviews/Duke-Dennis/2026-08-07_020002/critic.md` (SHA verified against context.json).

**Verdict:** trust strained, value high, recommendation **revise** — 2 blockers, 7 concerns.

**Blockers (both verified verbatim against the repo's Complex transcript, both one-sentence fixes):**
1. **"It stays in the drawer" is false per its own source.** In the same exchange, Duke says the shelved videos now go to his live channel — partly for the money. The draft reuses this false absolute as the load-bearing anti-Type-3 evidence.
2. **"He ruined a generation" is quote-distorted.** On the only verifiable tape, that sentence is Speedy's; Duke first says "I wouldn't say ruined it," then repeats it only when pressed. The draft prints it in quotes as Duke's flat assessment — and it carries the article title's claim.

**Strongest hit:** the article states its own falsifier and holds the four-year-stay paradox open instead of dissolving it ("His mother's sentence outlasted his own") — the credibility spine of the piece; preserve verbatim.

**Highest-priority concern:** the Union Square framing ("standing in somebody else's crowd") launders his agency — coverage shows he was arrested at the scene of AMP's own event and the dismissal was conditioned on a public apology. Also noteworthy: a search surfaced a publicly denied, unadjudicated allegation cluster the packet missed; the draft's exclusion is the responsible call, but the review flags it (CRITIC-Q1) so the precisely-scoped "only legal mark" sentence doesn't get broadened in revision.

